{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrxoZrwFYuifBD47mttb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The resolver error now names the parent that declared the broken dependency, so the ticket's case reads \"Unable to resolve flashinfer-python==0.6.8.post1 required by vllm: ...\" instead of pointing at its-hub. The test file passes (25/25, including the new regression test), and ruff check and format pass on both changed files. I did not commit.\n\n**Root cause:** `BootstrapRequirementResolver.resolve()` let the resolver's `ResolverException` escape without the parent. The failing dependency's name appeared in the message, but nothing said which package required it. The log line's prefix comes from the active top-level context, so the error looked like it belonged to its-hub.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `src/fromager/bootstrap_requirement_resolver.py`: `resolve()` wraps the `_resolve_and_extend()` call. When there is a `parent_req`, it re-raises `ResolverException` as `Unable to resolve {req} required by {parent_req}: {err}`, chained with `from err`. Top-level requirements (no parent) are re-raised unchanged.\n- `tests/test_bootstrap_requirement_resolver.py`: added `test_resolve_error_names_parent_requirement`. It mocks the sdist resolution to fail for `flashinfer-python==0.6.8.post1` with parent `vllm` and asserts the message names `vllm`.\n\n**Limits:**\n- `ENABLE_REPEATABLE_BUILD_MODE` doesn't appear anywhere under `src/`, `tests/`, `e2e/` or `docs/`. The fix sits in the shared resolve path, so it applies regardless of that flag, but I couldn't reproduce the exact mode from the ticket.\n- The message names only the immediate parent. For a deeper chain like its-hub → reward-hub → vllm, it says \"required by vllm\", not the full path. The full path is available from the `why` stack if you want it.\n- The prebuilt-wheel path (`wheels.resolve_all_prebuilt_wheels`) raises an `ExceptionGroup` with different text, so it isn't covered. I left it alone because it's a separate message format.\n- `mypy` isn't installed in `.venv` or on `PATH`, so I did not run the type check."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8012,"cache_read_input_tokens":123748,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8012},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e67d859c-50f9-456e-9ff0-55c53254d470","uuid":"9662e9eb-8e6d-4097-b1d8-4048bdd4b7a3","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:16:23.526Z","request_id":"req_011CfrxoZa4ih2AsyB6Ekvxg"}
